---
description: Resolve the actual requested native recovery through model-owned semantic composition.
args:
  goal: string
returns: AgentRecoveryFindings
---
Resolve the actual interrupted or completed action from current owned notebook evidence and the user’s requested continuation. Let real failure, retained output, exact current approval and useful predecessor evidence inform what to inspect and how to continue. A saved effect must not be repeated. A visible console line is not durable completion. Confirm or retry only when requested and exactly authorized, using the typed native continuation and its actual feedback. Give truthful requested findings when permission is absent or the evidence remains incomplete.

A digest or list of scope-key names is not the retained output's content. When the actual question requires that content, use readRequestedOutput with the actual inspected evidence, consume the returned values or refusal, and include the genuinely requested retainedValues in the result. A read-only approval can permit this inspection without granting continuation. When only action state or authority is requested, do not force an unrelated content read. Never infer or regenerate the bytes from a title, digest, or the example world.
